From accd8c3199d06d6364cb6d3572070f7a6565fd8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:03:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] audio: start a full device that was never started

mpv can freeze for good after an audio underrun with ao_alsa: video stops,
every thread idles in a futex, and the PCM sits in PREPARED with avail 0,
a full buffer that never starts. The log ends at "restarting audio after
underrun", with no "starting AO".

ao_alsa sets start_threshold to INT_MAX, so the device must be started
explicitly, and ao_play_data() starts it only right after a successful
write. The race:

1. ao_play_data() reads the state: RUNNING, with free space.
2. The underrun lands. audio_write()'s own recover_and_get_state() sees
   XRUN, calls snd_pcm_prepare(), and writes into the prepared PCM while
   p->streaming is still set, so no start follows.
3. The next pass reads PREPARED, takes the eof path, clears streaming and
   playing, and the core restarts audio.
4. The restart finds free_samples == 0 and returns before writing, so the
   start, which only follows a write, never comes.

Anything that delays the ao thread between steps 1 and 2 widens the
window. On an Allwinner H713 board, forced underrun #32 froze a run
(SIGSTOP 0.2-2 s each, tools/video/xrun-hammer.sh), while --ao=null
recovered 40 of 40.

When there is no space, mpv is playing and not paused or streaming, and
the device is not playing but holds queued data, start it. Nothing else
reaches that state. The code is unchanged on master as of 2026-10-02.
---
 audio/out/buffer.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/audio/out/buffer.c b/audio/out/buffer.c
index 037d2860f3..b93068d510 100644
--- a/audio/out/buffer.c
+++ b/audio/out/buffer.c
@@ -639,8 +639,24 @@ static bool ao_play_data(struct ao *ao)
 
     void **planes = NULL;
     int space = state.free_samples;
-    if (!space)
+    if (!space) {
+        // A full device that was never started. The driver's write() may
+        // recover from an underrun on its own (ao_alsa: XRUN -> prepare)
+        // and then queue data into the prepared device while p->streaming
+        // is still set, so no start follows. The underrun is then reported,
+        // streaming is cleared and playback restarted -- but the device is
+        // full, so nothing is written here and the start below, which only
+        // follows a write, never comes: a permanent stall with ALSA in
+        // PREPARED and avail 0. Start it.
+        if (!p->streaming && !state.playing && !p->paused &&
+            state.queued_samples > 0 && !ao->untimed)
+        {
+            MP_VERBOSE(ao, "starting AO (full but never started)\n");
+            ao->driver->start(ao);
+            p->streaming = true;
+        }
         return false;
+    }
     mp_assert(space >= 0);
 
     int samples = 0;
-- 
2.55.0

